        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.334,
            0.71,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": "How do we proceed with this problem? Here is a method."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.362,
            0.528,
            0.386
          ],
          "content": "What are the measures of $\\angle \\mathrm { B }$ and $\\angle \\mathrm { Y ? }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.394,
            0.724,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": "We know that the sum of the angles of a triangle is $1 8 0 ^ { \\circ } { \\textless }$ So $\\angle B + 35^{\\circ} + 75^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ},$ or $\\angle \\mathrm{B} + 110^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$ Thus, $\\angle \\mathrm{B} = 70^{\\circ}.$ Similarl $y , \\angle Y$ is also $7 0 ^ { \\circ } .$ Thus, we have $\\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{Y}.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.519,
            0.756,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": "? Does this help in showing that ΔABC and ΔXYZ are congruent?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.237,
            0.557,
            0.428,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.571,
            0.556,
            0.761,
            0.77
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.784,
            0.712,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": "These two triangles now satisfy the ASA condition with"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.469,
            0.804,
            0.557,
            0.861
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array} { r } { \\angle \\mathrm { B } = \\angle \\mathrm { Y } } \\\\ { \\mathrm { B C } = \\mathrm { Y Z } } \\\\ { \\angle \\mathrm { C } = \\angle \\mathrm { Z } . } \\end{array}",
          "image_source": "images/page_14_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.861,
            0.322,
            0.879
          ],
          "content": "So, $\\Delta \\mathrm { A B C } \\cong \\Delta \\mathrm { X Y Z } .$"
        },
